    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d720">

                <pb facs="0777" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1161</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-11-02T19:00:00+00:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 2, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 3, 8 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>961. Sir Edward Grey informs me that the Germans laid mine fields north of
                    Ireland from ships flying neutral flags. They are directly in the path of some
                    of the transatlantic liners and the <hi rendition="#italic">Olympic</hi> the
                    other day was in dangerous proximity to the mines. This danger constantly
                    spreads over a wider area.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
